-- Customer How-To page (how-to.html). Staff edit it under Page Text.
insert into public.pages (slug, lede_html, body_html) values
  ('how-to', '<p>Everything you need to use your pull list: sign in, add titles, follow your favorite series and artists, and pick up your books. Questions? Call us at {phone}.</p>', '<h2>1. Sign in (no password needed)</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="account.html">My Pull List</a> and type your email address.</li><li>Tap <strong>Email me a sign-in link</strong>. We''ll email you a link and a 6-digit code.</li><li>Tap the link, or type the code into the box on the page. You''re in, and you''ll stay signed in on that device.</li></ol><p>Don''t see the email? Check your spam folder. No account? You can still add titles as a guest with just your name and a phone number or email, but an account lets you change your list online and get reminders.</p><h2>2. Add titles to your pull list</h2><ol><li>Go to <a href="pre-orders.html">Pre-Orders</a> and browse upcoming books, toys and Funko Pops.</li><li>Tap <strong>Add to pull list</strong> on anything you want. The button changes to “✓ On your pull list.” Tap it again to take it off.</li><li>Some issues have several covers. <strong>Add all covers</strong> adds every regular cover at once (ratio and other limited incentive covers are not included).</li></ol><blockquote>Add titles by <strong>midnight on the Saturday</strong> before the order cutoff shown on each card. After that we''ve placed the order. If you miss it, call the shop and we''ll see what we can do.</blockquote><h2>3. Follow a series or artist</h2><p>Never miss an issue. Tap <strong>+ Follow</strong> on any card, then pick what to follow:</p><ul><li><strong>Series:</strong> every new issue is added to your pull list automatically.</li><li><strong>Cover artist:</strong> every cover that artist draws.</li><li><strong>Writer / artist:</strong> one cover of each issue they work on.</li></ul><p>See and change everything you follow on <a href="account.html">My Pull List</a> under <strong>Following</strong>. Unfollowing stops new titles from being added; titles already on your list stay until you remove them.</p><h2>4. Manage your pull list</h2><ul><li><strong>Change a quantity</strong> using the number next to the title. It saves right away. The limit is {max_copies_per_title} copies per title.</li><li><strong>Remove</strong> a title you no longer want. If a follow added it, it won''t come back.</li><li>You can make changes until the order cutoff. After that, call the shop.</li></ul><h2>5. Emails from us</h2><ul><li><strong>Weekly email:</strong> what''s coming and what''s on your list, plus a reminder before the cutoff.</li><li><strong>Ready for pickup:</strong> an email when your books are in.</li></ul><p>Both can be turned off any time in your profile on <a href="account.html">My Pull List</a>, or with the unsubscribe link at the bottom of any email.</p><h2>6. Pick up and pay</h2><p>Come in any time after your books arrive and pay at the counter. There''s nothing to pay online. We hold your books for {hold_days} days after they arrive, then release them back to stock.</p><p>Can''t make it in? Call us at {phone}. Some customers have their books shipped; ask us how.</p><h2>7. Your profile and privacy</h2><p>Update your name, phone and address any time under <strong>Profile</strong> on <a href="account.html">My Pull List</a>. To have your account and pull list removed completely, just ask us. See our <a href="privacy.html">privacy page</a>.</p>')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
